# Codebase Memory MCP index exclusions (gitignore syntax).
# .gitignore already applies; this adds paths that are tracked but should
# stay out of the code graph.

# Plaintext credentials, personal documents, sessions. secrets/ stays
# indexed: every file there is GPG-encrypted, and the layout shows where
# secrets live.
backups/
.env*
*.session
*.session-*

# Submodules (dotfiles/, jiyuu/, commonplace/) stay in the graph: boku is
# the monorepo, and cross-repo links (skills -> dotfiles, epics -> jiyuu
# code) need them in one project.
# Dependency and build output inside the submodules.
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/target/
**/dist/
# An untracked clone of grok-build (its own repo, 28 GB with build output)
# sits inside dotfiles. It was 138,000 of 214,000 nodes and isn't Boku code.
dotfiles/grok-build/
# Herdr fork: keep its own code (src/, crates/, scripts/, tests/) and drop
# the rest. vendor/ is vendored Ghostty (libghostty-vt, nearly all of the
# fork's Zig and C) plus a portable-pty copy, not code Unique maintains.
# docs/ is the .mdx site; assets/, packaging/ and distribution/ hold images
# and release packaging.
dotfiles/herdr/vendor/
dotfiles/herdr/docs/
dotfiles/herdr/assets/
dotfiles/herdr/packaging/
dotfiles/herdr/distribution/

# Generated Notion export copies that bury search results
epics/*/publication/

# Data files: JSON keys alone were ~170,000 of the graph's Variable nodes and
# buried code and prose. Keep scripts and Markdown; drop the data they read.
*.json
*.jsonl
*.csv
*.tsv
*.sql
*.log
**/data/**
**/evidence/**
**/saved-txs/**

# Images, PDFs, and rendered pages carry no code or prose worth linking.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.pdf
*.html
